well today kicks off black restaurant  week in las vegas the goal  is to promote the flavors of  african-american african and caribbean  cuisine  kate houston spoke with the owner of an  egyptian restaurant about how this event  helps give exposure to local eateries  here at potts they specialize in vegan  egyptian street food and by  participating in black restaurant week  they hope to introduce new flavors to  people across the valley  bringing uniqueness through food  it was always my my way  to bring my character out and to talk to  people through my food  iman hagag opened pot's egyptian  restaurant on rainbow in okie three  years ago  over the next week hagag will be  showcasing the fresh flavors of egyptian  food  which has greek french middle eastern  and indian influences  reaching a bigger audience and bigger  base for them to try it's it's it's a  way to reach out to more people  and learning about them learning about  us that community focus is one of the  main goals for black restaurant week  partner fallon farrell  the event started six years ago to  promote black owned restaurants across  the nation  and highlight the systemic barriers  facing business owners  this is the first year it's in las vegas  with a focus on helping businesses  recover from the pandemic  businesses in our community don't have  the cash flow  to do marketing campaigns so when the  door when the  finances start to tighten they can't go  and say okay well let me go  do this huge marketing campaign to  create more awareness  and so that's that's the problem that  we're solving potts will join many other  restaurants throughout the next week in  highlighting their most popular dishes  i think it's a really great thing to  reach out to different communities from  all over  and for vegas to participate in black  restaurant week i think it's a step  ahead kate houston  8 news now wow that food looked great  other restaurants that are going to be  participating include simply pure soul  food grits cafe  big chicken shack a whole lot more black  restaurant week by the way runs through  next sunday march 21st
 

